gibility-system operations govern further gains","Ceiling effects limit upside relative to lower-performing states"],"sourceContext":["https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/national-medicaid-chip-program-information/medicaid-chip-enrollment-data/monthly-medicaid-chip-application-eligibility-determination-and-enrollment-reports-data","https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/national-medicaid-chip-program-information/medicaid-chip-enrollment-data","https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c","https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/6165f45b-ca93-5bb5-9d06-db29c692a360"],"runAt":"2026-06-28T00:33:02Z","reasoning":[{"kind":"heading","text":"Forecast for Georgia Medicaid ex parte renewal share, August 2026"},{"kind":"text","text":"The resolver is a Georgia state row, not a national weighted average: the original first-publication August 2026 reporting-period row in the CMS eligibility processing dataset. The target is the share of completed Medicaid renewals processed ex parte, reported in percent and rounded to one decimal."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"official.lookup","call":"Inspected the registered CMS Medicaid PI target and local ledger identity fields for the Georgia August 2026 ex parte renewal-share resolver.","result":"Fetched canonical slug medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ga, unit percent, registered resolutionDate 2026-12-15, dataset id 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c, and dataPointId cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.ga.aug_2026."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"official.lookup","call":"Checked CMS Medicaid release vehicle context preserved for this data family.","result":"Fetched official release context that data.Medicaid.gov is updated monthly; inspected CMS page context listed Preliminary March 2026 data and June 26, 2026 as the current update date for related February 2026 and March 2026 entries."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"official.lookup","call":"Checked CMS eligibility-processing resolver fields used for this ex parte renewal-share target.","result":"Fetched original submission status O, August 2026 reporting period, numerator as completed renewals processed through ex parte renewal, denominator as total completed renewals, and expected publication lag of about 3 to 4 months after the reporting period."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"repo.lookup","call":"Read the local official-source-derived Georgia historical context for this exact CMS series.","result":"Fetched Georgia values: 2025-07 = 77.3 percent, 2025-09 = 78.2 percent, 2025-11 = 81.1 percent, 2026-01 = 82.2 percent, and 2026-02 = 81.6 percent."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"repo.lookup","call":"Computed recent Georgia movement and latest-value anchor from the inspected sample.","result":"Fetched latest inspected Georgia value 2026-02 = 81.6 percent; changes were +0.9 percentage points from 2025-07 to 2025-09, +2.9 from 2025-09 to 2025-11, +1.1 from 2025-11 to 2026-01, and -0.6 from 2026-01 to 2026-02."},{"kind":"text","text":"Base-rate/reference class: the most relevant outside view is Georgia's own recent first-print run for this CMS eligibility-processing series. The five observed points average 80.1 percent, the latest three average 81.6 percent, and the latest inspected value is 81.6 percent, so latest-value persistence with modest trend continuation is the prior."},{"kind":"text","text":"Level, momentum, and mechanism: Georgia is already a high ex parte performer, so ceiling effects matter. The July-to-January improvement supports a mild upward update, but the February dip and high starting level argue against extrapolating the full 2025 trend through August."},{"kind":"text","text":"Prior/update/interval: prior model is Georgia latest-value persistence with damped local trend, using five inspected observations from 2025-07, 2025-09, 2025-11, 2026-01, and 2026-02. Starting from latest inspected 81.6 percent, I add +1.4 pp for the 2025-to-early-2026 improvement signal and +0.6 pp for CMS compliance and continued automation drift, yielding 83.6. The 80% interval is calibrated from realized first-print movements and widened for the six-month horizon, renewal-cohort mix, and limited skipped-month sample, giving 78.2 to 88.9."},{"kind":"text","text":"Counter-consideration: the forecast could be too high if the 2026-01 and 2026-02 values already represent Georgia's practical ceiling or if August has a manual-heavy renewal cohort. Upside outside the interval would require a durable system or data-match improvement pushing the first print above 88.9 percent; downside outside the interval would require a data-source outage, eligibility-system issue, reporting break, or cohort mix pushing the share below 78.2 percent."},{"kind":"math","text":"Historical mean = (77.3 + 78.2 + 81.1 + 82.2 + 81.6) / 5 = 80.1 percent. Adjacent changes were +0.9, +2.9, +1.1, and -0.6 pp, with mean absolute change about 1.4 pp. Point calculation: 81.6 latest inspected value + 1.4 pp damped trend + 0.6 pp automation/compliance drift = 83.6 percent. Interval calculation: center 83.6, lower half-width 5.4 pp and upper half-width 5.3 pp, yielding 78.2 to 88.9 after one-decimal rounding."},{"kind":"text","text":"Resolution-date note: the canonical ledger target uses 2026-12-15, tied to CMS's monthly data.Medicaid.gov release vehicle for a three-to-four-month-lag August 2026 first print. I did not find a separate future-dated CMS placeholder in this sandbox; I keep the target's date and bind scoring to the first official CMS dataset print."},{"kind":"forecast","point":83.6,"ciLow":78.2,"ciHigh":88.9}]}
