ntage points around the point, skewed upward for apartment-project lumpiness, giving -10.0% to +16.0%.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Counter-consideration and scenarios: downside outside the interval would be another large apartment-project drop or delayed approvals pushing the print below -10.0%; upside outside the interval would be a renewed multi-unit approval surge like February, above +16.0%; the central case is a partial rebound with no repeat of February's one-off jump.\"},{\"kind\":\"forecast\",\"point\":2.0,\"ciLow\":-10.0,\"ciHigh\":16.0}]}"}}
